  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have $n=4$ rectangles. Using the left Riemann sum, the area is approximated as\n\n$$\nA≈f(-3)Δ{x}_{1}+f(-1)Δ{x}_{2}+f(0)Δ{x}_{3}+f(3)Δ{x}_{4},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the next one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{x}_{i}={x}_{i+1}-{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δx$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δx$ | $2$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $-$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈-1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-2+1+6+8 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
